<title>NETHERLANDS: First draft of Fokker rescue plan rejected - paper.</title>
<headline>First draft of Fokker rescue plan rejected - paper.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch government has demanded changes to a letter of intent from South Korea's Samsung Aerospace to buy bankrupt plane maker Fokker, newspaper Het Financieele Dagblad said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Quoting sources close to the negotiations, the paper said the government was asking for more concrete guarantees on the number of Dutch jobs that will be saved and how much of the new 130-seater aircraft production would remain in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>It said Samsung had agreed to come up with another proposal and that a deal was expected to be sealed before this weekend.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
